{{Codex|Echo nature's violent beauty with this special Tigris.}}
The '''Sancti Tigris''' is a {{Weapon|Tigris}} variant available only from {{Faction|New Loka}}. Featuring increased damage, reload speed, and [[critical chance]] at the cost of lowered critical damage and accuracy, the Sancti Tigris also comes with an innate [[Purity]] effect.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Can use the Tigris-exclusive {{M|Combat Reload}} mod.
*Innate [[multishot]] of 6 pellets.
*Unique trigger type allows for two rapid shots against tough targets, or careful shot management against many weaker opponents. First shot on button press, the second on button release.
*Innate [[Purity]] effect.
*Innate {{Pol|Vazarin}}, {{Pol|Madurai}}, and {{Pol|Naramon}} polarities.

{{Advantages|class=Shotgun|
*Third highest damage of all primary shotguns, behind {{Weapon|Tigris Prime}} and {{Weapon|Exergis}}.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Shotgun|
*Has linear damage falloff from 100% to 42.86% from 8m to 20m target distance (distances are affected by [[Projectile Speed]]).
*Extremely low magazine size of just two rounds; requires frequent reloading.
*Low pellet count.
*Inefficient against groups, unless using [[Punch Through]] mods.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Tigris}}
{{WeaponComparison|Tigris Prime|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
*The Sancti Tigris can be acquired by reaching the Rank of '''Flawless''' with {{Faction|New Loka}}, and spending {{sc|125,000}} to purchase. As with all Syndicate Weapons, the Sancti Tigris cannot be chosen as the free offering upon ranking up to Flawless rank.
*Syndicate weapons can also be acquired via [[Trade System|Trading]], but only for unranked copies without [[Forma]] and [[Orokin Catalyst]] installed.
*Players must have a [[Mastery Rank]] of at least 12 to acquire the Sancti Tigris, either through trading or through the Syndicates themselves.

==Tips==
*The {{PAGENAME}} has a high chance of cutting corpses into pieces, making it an ideal choice for a [[Desecrate|Desecrating]] {{WF|Nekros}} to bring along, as the game considers the cut corpses as separate entities, essentially giving multiple corpses to desecrate from a single enemy and thus yielding more chances to create more drops.
*While the Sancti Tigris is less effective against targets vulnerable to {{D|Puncture}} and {{D|Impact}} damage types, it still deals an obscene amount of damage against targets with these resistances, dealing more damage than some weapon's primary damage types.
*The innate {{Pol|Vazarin}} polarity matches for {{M|Tainted Shell}}; this mod has a high capacity requirement but is very efficient on the Tigris as the duplex trigger is hardly affected by the fire rate drawback.
**The decrease in fire rate increases the delay before the Tigris automatically reloads after emptying its magazine. This can be remedied by pressing the Reload button right after firing the second shot.

==Trivia==
*The first part of its name, Sancti, is likely derived from the Latin word "sanctus", meaning holy. The Sanctus is also the name of a hymn in Catholic liturgy, or 'Hymn of Victory' in the Greek rendition.

