{{Codex|The sidearm of choice for Prime Grineer warriors, Sagek Prime blends Grineer brutality with Orokin aesthetics. When Sagek Prime inflicts a critical hit, its next shot has a chance to gain significant Status Chance.}}
'''Sagek Prime''' is a standalone [[Prime]] automatic sidearm used by ancient [[Orokin Era]] {{Faction|Grineer}} soldiers. Despite its near-nonexistent [[Status Chance]], [[Critical Hit]]s from the Sagek Prime have a chance for its next shot to apply 5 Status Effects.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*[[Critical Hit]]s have a '''6%''' chance to set the next shot's [[Status Chance]] to '''500%'''.
**The effect is triggered separately for each bullet when using [[Multishot]], as well as each enemy hit with [[Punch Through]].
***Whether an enemy hit via Punch Through can be subject to the increased status chance depends on whether or not the previous enemy hit was critically hit, not whether the previous shot did.
**Chance remains until landing another successful shot; missed shots will not reset the chance.
**Set status chance ignores all other modifiers, whether from mods or Warframe abilities.
**Even though the '''500%''' chance inflicts '''5''' procs, it does '''not''' trigger {{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}} more than once.
*Innate one {{Pol|Madurai}} and one {{Pol|Naramon}} polarities.
{{Advantages}}

{{Disadvantages}}

{{Acquisition|Sagek Prime's main and component blueprints are obtained from Rotation A of [[The Perita Rebellion]], available after completing [[The Old Peace]] quest.

Alternatively Sagek Prime's blueprints can be purchased from [[Roathe]] in [[La Cathėdrale]], [[Sanctum Anatomica]] for {{Resource|Maphica}} obtained in [[The Descendia]]. Each component blueprint requires 25 and the main blueprint requires 35, totaling 85 Maphica for the whole set.}}

==Crafting==
Sagek Prime's materials are obtained from [[The Perita Rebellion]]. A total of 1,400 {{Resource|Agnovidisc}}, 380 {{Resource|Laudavi}}, and 175 {{Resource|Servoris}} are needed to craft both parts.

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon|name=Sagek Prime}}

==Notes==
* The parts '''cannot''' be sold for {{Resource|Orokin Ducats}}.
*Both {{Weapon|Galariak Prime}} and {{Weapon|Sagek Prime}} only appear in [[Duviri]] AFTER obtaining the weapons. (Bug?)

==Trivia==
*The Sagek Prime's passive ability is essentially the opposite of the [[Gotva Prime|Gotva Prime's]] passive ability. 
*Despite having Prime in the name, [[Baro Ki'Teer]] will not interact with the player as he would if you had primes equipped.
